# Local dev config. Copy to .env and fill in what you need — every var here
# is optional; anything unset falls back to its documented default (see
# server/internal/config/config.go). A real exported env var always wins
# over .env. Never commit .env itself (it's gitignored).

# Public origin the app is served from. Drives cookie Secure/__Host- mode,
# the checkOrigin CSRF check, and links in emails. Needed for `make dev`
# (already set there via the Makefile) — only set it here if you're running
# `go run ./server` directly instead of through `make dev`.
# APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# Telegram sign-in. Get a token from @BotFather on Telegram; the numeric id
# before the ":" is derived automatically and exposed (non-secret) on
# GET /api/health for the frontend's Login Widget button.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=123456789:AAneed-the-real-token-here

# SMTP. Leave unset to use LogMailer (verify/reset links print to stdout
# instead of being emailed — the normal way to develop locally).
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.example.com
# SMTP_PORT=587
# SMTP_USER=postmaster@example.com
# SMTP_PASS=change-me
# SMTP_FROM=no-reply@example.com
# SMTP_FROM_NAME=Српски
